{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other","id":1009776,"title":"How do Changelings and Mages feel about each other?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-29T07:31:53-08:00","id":1009776,"title":"How do Changelings and Mages feel about each other?","content":"I was curious if any of the official books ever said anything on this topic, and if not what do you guys think about it: how do Changelings and Mages feel about each other? Under what circumstances do you think it would be most likely for them to be friends or enemies? Do Mages connected to the watchtower in Arcadia (Acanthus) tend to have a different relationship with Changelings than the other four types of mages? Also, I assume Changelings are not considered &quot;Sleepers&quot;, even though they are not Awakened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T07:58:31-08:00","id":1009788,"title":"","content":"I'm sure there's something buried somewhere in the different supplements- Changeling has quite a few of them. Changelings for sure count a Sleepwalkers- anyone with a single Supernatural Merit does, so Major Templates easily qualify. As far as I can recall off the top of my head, the conversation usually involves a lot of cross-talking, seeing as the two Arcadias are only superficially and thematically similar, but both Mages and Changelings tend to not be aware of this fact. At least not initially. This can lead to a good deal of hilarity.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage/Changeling: </b>Yeah, I went to Arcadia and came out changed. There were shenanigans involving Fate and screwy timelines. Wait, you too?<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling to Mage: </b>How did you get out?<br /> <br /> <b>Mage to Changeling: </b>How can I get back?<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling to Mage: </b>Why on earth would you ever want to do that?!<br /> <br /> Extra hilarity ensues if the Mage actually tries to <i>walk </i>to Arcadia/Faerie through the Hedge once they find out they can do that. They would likely rather quickly realize this isn't what they signed up for... and then find that they have no conventional way out. Sure, with a Fate spell they could presumably open a Hedge Gate much as a Spirit spell can open a Locus/Verge and a Death spell can open an Avernian Gateway, but first they have to <i>find </i>one first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:31:57-08:00","id":1009801,"title":"","content":"It depends on the individuals in question. For some changelings a mages ability to pretty much reshape reality at will might seem suspiciously similar to what the Gentry were doing in Arcadia, and the use of the same name to describe a similar realm of power for mages doesn't really help their case here. A lot of mages also tend to be overly curious/nosy about new supernatural things, so that might also get on some changelings nerves.<br /> <br /> That said, assuming they get past any misunderstandings and whatnot, they're quite capable of functioning on friendly terms. A mage could prove quite the valuable asset given their ability spread, especially considering a lot of them asking relatively little (from the changelings perspective) in return; small trinkets, permission to ask questions about various things concerning changeling nature and being allowed to observe/study their powers/habits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 11-29-2016, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:45:00-08:00","id":1009807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009788#post1009788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure there's something buried somewhere in the different supplements- Changeling has quite a few of them. Changelings for sure count a Sleepwalkers- anyone with a single Supernatural Merit does, so Major Templates easily qualify. As far as I can recall off the top of my head, the conversation usually involves a lot of cross-talking, seeing as the two Arcadias are only superficially and thematically similar, but both Mages and Changelings tend to not be aware of this fact. At least not initially. This can lead to a good deal of hilarity.<br /> <br /> <b>Mage/Changeling: </b>Yeah, I went to Arcadia and came out changed. There were shenanigans involving Fate and screwy timelines. Wait, you too?<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling to Mage: </b>How did you get out?<br /> <br /> <b>Mage to Changeling: </b>How can I get back?<br /> <br /> <b>Changeling to Mage: </b>Why on earth would you ever want to do that?!<br /> <br /> Extra hilarity ensues if the Mage actually tries to <i>walk </i>to Arcadia/Faerie through the Hedge once they find out they can do that. They would likely rather quickly realize this isn't what they signed up for... and then find that they have no conventional way out. Sure, with a Fate spell they could presumably open a Hedge Gate much as a Spirit spell can open a Locus/Verge and a Death spell can open an Avernian Gateway, but first they have to <i>find </i>one first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are there two Arcadias? The description in the Mage book sounds like the Changeling Arcadia to me?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12390-gadren","name":"gadren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:51:33-08:00","id":1009811,"title":"","content":"The first thing worth noting is that no Acanthus would mistake the Arcadia they Awakened to with the Arcadia the changelings escape from-the thorns around the Lunargent tower are very notably cracks in time, silvery, glowing cracks of branching, clawing possibility. Changelings might not pick up on that right away, but give a mage time to talk and they'll be able to pick up on the differences.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, it depends on the nature of the relationship. Changelings are a good source of Mysteries(most small scale, sure, but still), but aren't too keen to being looked into. That said, they do tend to keep their eyes open for weird shit too, in the interest of raising as many tin-cans on string they can to let them know when the True Fae are coming, so investigating strange sites is something they have in common, and Kenning can, in a lot of certain ways, can provide information that Mage Sight doesn't do. While they might clash over mundane resources like anyone else, mages and changelings occult resources don't immediately overlap, although mage's abilities to tie their spells to sleepwalkers can be lead egregious interventions if those walkers turn out to be someone from the changeling's past. On the other hand, mages are good people to have in your corner, and they probably qualify for Bargains.<br /> <br /> As has been said, it largely depends on the nature of their relationship, how it was established and the circumstances that define it. There's reason for them to poke into one another's business, and to be enemies, but there's also just as much cause for some good alliances, and even more cause for them to mostly keep to themselves, barring those times they bump into each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:54:09-08:00","id":1009812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gadren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009807#post1009807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are there two Arcadias? The description in the Mage book sounds like the Changeling Arcadia to me?</div> </div> </div> </div>Second Edition largely has done away with the cosmology teasing, to a point where it's definitive unless you <i>really</i> want it to be the opposite-Changeling and Mage Arcadia's are two completely different places.<br /> <br /> It helps that Mage Arcadia is <i>not a place </i>at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T08:56:52-08:00","id":1009815,"title":"","content":"It can <i>almost</i> be a place if a Lustrum is projected in the area, which is what the Watchtowers <i>do</i>, but yes, cArcadia and mArcadia are explicitly not the same place in 2e.<br /> <br /> (This hasn't stopped me from making them related places in my games, though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:19:45-08:00","id":1009828,"title":"","content":"Well I seriously doubt they're <i>not </i>related in <i>any </i>way, seeing as there's too much symbolic overlap, but that's kind of like saying the Shadow and the Hedge are the same place because they're both places where reflections of the real world become distorted based on human feelings.<br /> <br /> That being said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> didn't you do up a really pretty cosmology map that is posted somewhere on the forums where most of the Invisible Realms are Fallen reflections of Emanation Realms? I ended up saving the image when I stumbled across it, because it was gorgeous, but I have no idea how to attach images, and don't want to step on your toes by posting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:28:22-08:00","id":1009831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009828#post1009828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I seriously doubt they're <i>not </i>related in <i>any </i>way, seeing as there's too much symbolic overlap, but that's kind of like saying the Shadow and the Hedge are the same place because they're both places where reflections of the real world become distorted based on human feelings.<br /> <br /> That being said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar99_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"99\" data-vbnamecard=\"99\">ArcaneArts</a> didn't you do up a really pretty cosmology map that is posted somewhere on the forums where most of the Invisible Realms are Fallen reflections of Emanation Realms? I ended up saving the image when I stumbled across it, because it was gorgeous, but I have no idea how to attach images, and don't want to step on your toes by posting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I posted the work of someone else that was very pretty and god-awfully wrong. I did it because it was pretty and we could all chat about how wrong it was. Led to some fun story ideas built on the fact it was so wrong.<br /> <br /> I neither do nor believe in cosmology maps <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/121410-new-game-for-2015?p=138948#post138948\">Here's where the joking happens.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 11-29-2016, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T09:43:29-08:00","id":1009834,"title":"","content":"Also, the Arcadia Question has been a pain in the ass of Changeling so damn long. Mage never gave much of a shit about it, but Changeling wasted so much text on the cocktease, pages that could have honestly been put to better use for other things. Mage's team began pushing to keep their Arcadia seperate since Imperial Mysteries(where honestly the problem was solved anyways), and when Changeling went into development, one of the most emphatic footnotes in the initial development was &quot;Changeling Arcadia is not Mage Arcadia. We are not wasting words on this again.&quot;*<br /> <br /> Truthfully, from the Mage perspective, Changeling Arcadia is a place that resonates with pretty much all of the Supernal Realms anyways. Hell, Pandemonium is equally as strong a factor in cArcadia as mArcadia is. In my own headcanon, a Mage is going to need Fate+Mind for pretty much any digging into the area.<br /> <br /> *Paraphasing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T14:50:36-08:00","id":1009947,"title":"","content":"What about the theory that the Arcadia of the True Fae is merely a shadow of the true Supernal Arcadia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T14:58:28-08:00","id":1009951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009947#post1009947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about the theory that the Arcadia of the True Fae is merely a shadow of the true Supernal Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is no meaningful distinction between Faerie and a particularly auspicious gambling den in that regard.<br /> <br /> Arcadia is collectively the Timeyest and Fateyest portions of the Supernal World that mages experience, and Faerie is a particularly Timey and Fatey chunk of Phenomenal reality. Whether the relation of those levels of Arcana concentration is one of dilution or distillation is academic, because neither place experiences time in the same fashion as the material world and both places are sufficiently hostile to non-naturalized humanlike entities that figuring out if one pre-dates the other is the stuff of an entire chronicle at best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:08:22-08:00","id":1009957,"title":"","content":"In my chronicle, those mages who are aware of the Faerie Arcadia tend to subscribe to this theory, but it may or may not be true. Neither mages nor changelings know for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T15:19:56-08:00","id":1009965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009957#post1009957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my chronicle, those mages who are aware of the Faerie Arcadia tend to subscribe to this theory, but it may or may not be true. Neither mages nor changelings know for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do What Thou Wilt at your table is the whole of the rule there.<br /> <br /> Some of us have different concerns.<br /> <br /> Anyways, even if for some reason cArcadia is a shadow of mArcadia, that still distinctly makes it two places, not one, and realistically cArcadia just doesn't operate like mArcadia beyond the basics. There's a nuance to the details that keep them separate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T16:21:14-08:00","id":1009991,"title":"","content":"The only way to solve the question of the Arcadias is, of course, for them to fight. Two Arcadia enter, one Arcadia leave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T16:35:10-08:00","id":1009993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009991#post1009991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only way to solve the question of the Arcadias is, of course, for them to fight. Two Arcadia enter, one Arcadia leave.</div> </div> </div> </div>mArcadia unfortunately has a heavy advantage on that one, considering that that Arcadia enters/entered/will enter the arena, dies/died/will die and keep on going until it wins/won/will win and leaves/left/will leave.<br /> <br /> cArcadia is <i>screwy</i> but not <i>that</i><i> screwy</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T16:38:57-08:00","id":1009995,"title":"","content":"What if Changeling Arcadia transformed Mage Arcadia into (a) Changeling Arcadia, and Mage Arcadia causes Changeling Arcadia to Awaken as (a) Mage Arcadia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T17:01:05-08:00","id":1009999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009995#post1009995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Changeling Arcadia transformed Mage Arcadia into (a) Changeling Arcadia, and Mage Arcadia causes Changeling Arcadia to Awaken as (a) Mage Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Just no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T17:03:24-08:00","id":1010000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009999#post1009999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. Just no.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yesssss. It's the only (il)logical conclusion to be drawn from this contest. Role reversal/role inversion/infinite mirror hallway of hot Arcadia-on-Arcadia action!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T17:30:23-08:00","id":1010008,"title":"","content":"I just have head-canon that both Arcadias are from the same instance of Arcadia, but were split into alternate versions of one another. M!Arcadia became an integrated part of the supernal realms, while C!Arcadia developed into the Hedge and, in stealing people, integrated itself as part of the cosmology at large. Both realms embody fate and time, and both embed parts of themselves into mortals (Mages and Changelings) but their methodologies are...decidedly different.<br /> <br /> Or, to put it in a metaphor, the two Arcadias are twins - they have many aspects that are superficially similar and are part of the same universe, but they are two entities with their own identities, methods and, ultimately, influences upon the mortal realm.<br /> <br /> Of course, I don't know a lot about Mage, much less its version of Arcadia, so I could be kinda off here. :-p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T17:31:35-08:00","id":1010009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009995#post1009995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if Changeling Arcadia transformed Mage Arcadia into (a) Changeling Arcadia, and Mage Arcadia causes Changeling Arcadia to Awaken as (a) Mage Arcadia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it already happened, and no one can tell the difference... * gains the Paranoid Condition","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T18:04:16-08:00","id":1010017,"title":"","content":"Now I'm having a headache about an Arcadian Verge in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> You people are not good people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T19:14:55-08:00","id":1010032,"title":"","content":"I believe it's belong the lines of &quot;as long as you promise to put away the magical dissection tools, I'll refrain from stabbing you until you get on my nerves again.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-29T21:47:27-08:00","id":1010053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gadren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other#post1009776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was curious if any of the official books ever said anything on this topic, and if not what do you guys think about it: how do Changelings and Mages feel about each other? Under what circumstances do you think it would be most likely for them to be friends or enemies? Do Mages connected to the watchtower in Arcadia (Acanthus) tend to have a different relationship with Changelings than the other four types of mages? Also, I assume Changelings are not considered &quot;Sleepers&quot;, even though they are not Awakened.</div> </div> </div> </div>My general answer about this is that Changelings and Mages don't like each other on first blush but they are, when actually engaging one another, more likely to be friends than enemies; they simply have too many ways to be mutually beneficial for anything but friendly interaction to constitute the majority of proper interaction, even if only to a slim degree.<br /> <br /> Mages <i>crave</i> the things Changelings have. Changelings give them access to whole new areas of magical study otherwise unavailable to them. Changelings can produce odd magical trinkets, curious and impossible baubles, and the ever-unusual goblin fruit for a Mage to study, all with (relatively) minimal effort.<br /> <br /> Changelings, meanwhile, can always use the staggering firepower a Mage represents. Even a novice Mage has a degree of acuity and diversity with their magic that dwarfs most other forms of supernatural ally, and all they ask in exchange is a chance to stare at you oddly for a few minutes. For most supernaturals, the odd demands of a Mage to get to analyze someone or for a bit of their hair or what have you might seem strange, but for Changelings, it's literally just another trip to the Market.<br /> <br /> None of this means that any individual Mage is trustworthy, though, and once a Mage finds out the Lost exist, the Lost get no sleep until their curiosity is satisfied. No amount of threats or bribery will allay their rampant thirst for knowledge. Likewise, sorcerers aren't usually keen to approach anything at a disadvantage; even the most freedom-loving libertine or thearch prefers in their heart to have a position of extreme strength when approaching anything. As such, the first meetings are usually exceptionally frosty for the Awakened and exceptionally intrusive and suspicious for the Changeling.<br /> <br /> Acanthus aren't any more connected to Changelings than any other Mage, but their first meetings probably go far more smoothly than those of other Paths. An Acanthus knows a Changeling's perspective somewhat; unhinged from Time and beholding the vast weave of Fate. They know what it's like to be bound to odd laws and strange rules. That makes it easier to understand their perspectives. The downside is that the similarities turn uncanny when an Acanthus finds out that the bargains empowering a Changeling aren't with with any entity as the Acanthus would understand it, thus creating a problem of comprehension that is not easily solved.<br /> <br /> Thyrsus also kinda get along for that reason; they're in the &quot;We know odd rules and have strange urges&quot; support group too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T01:46:21-08:00","id":1010107,"title":"","content":"Acanthus are both terrifying and uniquely useful to changelings for the same reason they are so to Demons: With sufficient Fate magic, oaths, pacts and contracts become optional.<br /> <br /> Need a friend who can no-sell an enemy changeling's contracts, or rewrite a soul pact's terms? Go get an Acanthus. But they can do it to you, too, so it's a last resort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T01:49:26-08:00","id":1010109,"title":"","content":"But, that's no different to a werewolf pack dealing with a Thyrsus - sure, she can control the Gauntlet, produce Essence on demand and rewrite spirits' natures. That makes her either a valuable packmate or the worst enemy the pack's ever faced, depending on how the meeting goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T04:43:58-08:00","id":1010151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1010109#post1010109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, that's no different to a werewolf pack dealing with a Thyrsus - sure, she can control the Gauntlet, produce Essence on demand and rewrite spirits' natures. That makes her either a valuable packmate or the worst enemy the pack's ever faced, depending on how the meeting goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Crossover Chronicle cannot come soon enough.<br /> <br /> BTW, who will be the developer? I also hope both you and the people who were involved in the great crossover portions of The Pack and Demon Storyteller's Guide are involved in the project.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T06:48:26-08:00","id":1010183,"title":"","content":"ArcaneArts: I agree. It's just a theory that some mages have advanced in-game. The main reason I chose not to make this theory black-letter law in my campaign is because of something a lot of people on these forums have complained about<b></b>: the idea of making Mage the center of the universe and having everything else revolve around it. I like Mage: the Awakening very much, but I wanted to avoid falling into that trap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:57:29-08:00","id":1010219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1010053#post1010053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The downside is that the similarities turn uncanny when an Acanthus finds out that the bargains empowering a Changeling aren't with with any entity as the Acanthus would understand it, thus creating a problem of comprehension that is not easily solved.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, did you mean this as a downside for the Mage? Because to my Mage-player eyes this reads &quot;Big, gnarly Mystery that's gonna get me loads of Arcane Beats to work through&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1909-juhn","name":"Juhn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T08:58:43-08:00","id":1010220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1010017#post1010017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm having a headache about an Arcadian Verge in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> You people are not good people.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my head, it's like an old Bugs Bunny routine, where two elegant sylvan nightmares stand staring at each other; mimicking each other's actions like a mirror in increasingly elaborate ways, until they each pick up an anvil, hold it above their heads, and let it go. Only one falls because only one of them was able to use their magic to make something improbable happen with cold iron.<br /> <br /> Tha-a-tha-a-that's a cosmological horror story, folks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T10:53:20-08:00","id":1010263,"title":"","content":"As Brookshaw pointed out, a lot of it is the context of how the twain interact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T12:08:06-08:00","id":1010294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1009831#post1009831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I posted the work of someone else that was very pretty and god-awfully wrong. I did it because it was pretty and we could all chat about how wrong it was. Led to some fun story ideas built on the fact it was so wrong.<br /> <br /> I neither do nor believe in cosmology maps <i>at all</i>.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/121410-new-game-for-2015?p=138948#post138948&amp;quot;]Here's</a> where the joking happens.[/URL]</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that is a pretty map. I can see a Mage coming up with this, maybe even believing it's correct. Just because Mages have the tools to explore and learn of the vastness of their reality and existence, doesn't mean people will necessarily come to the same conclusions or viewpoints. <br /> <br /> I would note that it might be rather difficult to map multiple dimensions or states of being on a 2D plane, though... I like the vibe of &quot;Here be dragons&quot;, I gotta say...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:28:36-08:00","id":1010325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1010294#post1010294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow, that is a pretty map. I can see a Mage coming up with this, maybe even believing it's correct. Just because Mages have the tools to explore and learn of the vastness of their reality and existence, doesn't mean people will necessarily come to the same conclusions or viewpoints.<br /> <br /> I would note that it might be rather difficult to map multiple dimensions or states of being on a 2D plane, though... I like the vibe of &quot;Here be dragons&quot;, I gotta say...</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the conversation that follows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-30T13:41:05-08:00","id":1010329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1010325#post1010325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the conversation that follows.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did and it was interesting. There were a variety of ideas going around. Some of them mentioning of Mages arguing about how the map is inaccurate.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of some of the really old maps of the world that early cartographers made. Made with some basis but through perception, bias, or poor tools, not quite what we're familiar with. And that's really fascinating to see what people thought of the world they were in. <br /> <br /> I could see Mages arguing about how that particular map must be incorrect because of some detail, and other Mages arguing about how it must be correct because of some other detail. But that's because I really like Mages to focus on Mystery, so I do love Mages having strong opinions. And sometimes, they might even be onto something. ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"u