/div> <div class=\"message\">I am so confused, but it may be because it's after midnight and I have a headache</div> </div> </div> </div>The Arcadia problem has a notional neighbor in nomenclatural tangles: There are about six wildly different varieties of being in the Chronicles of Darkness that are all called &quot;demons&quot; at least some of the time.<br /> <br /> Two of them explicitly hate each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T00:51:43-08:00","id":1012436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1012432#post1012432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arcadia problem has a notional neighbor in nomenclatural tangles: There are about six wildly different varieties of being in the Chronicles of Darkness that are all called &quot;demons&quot; at least some of the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then lucifuge also consider everything that is ephemeral as demons....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:00:17-08:00","id":1013129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1012395#post1012395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, if we really wanted to get worse, we'd shift the dialogue over to demons.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah its like my demons are haunted by demons.<br /> <br /> A Dearheart Darkling (described as Succubi/Incubi) enters the dreams of an Unchained Demon only to find a confused Onieros Succubus discussing the weird thing happened to the dreamer she was feeding on with a demonic Goetia of Sinful Vice who suggests they go ask a Supernal Imp in a nearby Supernal Verge in the Astral Plane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:05:23-08:00","id":1013133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1012432#post1012432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arcadia problem has a notional neighbor in nomenclatural tangles: There are about six wildly different varieties of being in the Chronicles of Darkness that are all called &amp;quot;demons&amp;quot; at least some of the time.<br /> <br /> Two of them explicitly hate each other.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which two explicited hate each other?<br /> <br /> Okay here is my list of 2e demons, Unchained, Supernal Imps, Supernal Wraiths, Oneiros Succubi, Oneiros Incubi, Lower Depths demons, some Goetics might be called demons, Lucifuge.<br /> <br /> Are you talking about Changelings and True Fae who sometimes take on demonic forms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T07:38:42-08:00","id":1013153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1010107#post1010107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Acanthus are both terrifying and uniquely useful to changelings for the same reason they are so to Demons: With sufficient Fate magic, oaths, pacts and contracts become optional.<br /> <br /> Need a friend who can no-sell an enemy changeling's contracts, or rewrite a soul pact's terms? Go get an Acanthus. But they can do it to you, too, so it's a last resort.</div> </div> </div> </div> An Acanthus who does that too much and too carelessly is going to wind up with alot of strange enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T09:15:13-08:00","id":1013217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1013133#post1013133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which two explicited hate each other?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons of the Lower Depths and &quot;demons&quot; of the Abyss. There's a whole section in Inferno about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:06:53-08:00","id":1013245,"title":"","content":"Jonathan Strange and Mr. Norrell works surprisingly well as an Awakening/Lost crossover, right down to Mages thinking they've got all the answers and failing to realize that the Gentry be trippin' yo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T10:07:53-08:00","id":1013246,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah. But that's 1e. Of course the same could be true in 2e, perhaps we will find out in Signs of Sorcery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-13T19:54:57-08:00","id":1016876,"title":"","content":"And now... the voice of dissent. Changelings and mages, to me, seem to actually be opposites.<br /> <br /> Its no secret that Mages are considered the creme de le creme of supernaturals. They're 1%, the elite, the privileged people that look down on other supernaturals. They're encouraged to use their magic to bind subjects to study and analyze for their obsessions. Their very presence warps the world around them. Literally - their nimbus is pulling down parts of the Supernal and overwriting reality bit by bit, and you're slowly transforming people via Nimbus Tilt. Changelings, meanwhile, are defined by -fleeing- from the Gentry - magically privileged beings that shape the realm around them at whim. They're the ones that were the subjected to all the things that mages are inclined to do.<br /> <br /> In a very real way, the Awakened are like humanized versions of the Gentry. And changelings bear striking similarities to the entities that mages bind to their purpose. Now, at high Wisdom/Clarity, you can see the difference - both mages and changelings are still people, unlike the Gentry/bound spirits. However, the less Wise / perceptive lose sight of that, and the sympathy breaks down. Fate magic, by all rights, should be horrifying to changelings. The Lost rely on pledges being relatively consistant for mental stability. Mages can throw that out the window. Meanwhile, changelings are extremely slippery, avoiding magic and any attempts to hold them still for study. <br /> <br /> This all creates a far more complicated relationship than just meeting up and then possibly getting along after some misunderstandings at the nature of Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T03:26:22-08:00","id":1018399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1016876#post1016876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now... the voice of dissent. Changelings and mages, to me, seem to actually be opposites.<br /> <br /> Its no secret that Mages are considered the creme de le creme of supernaturals. They're 1%, the elite, the privileged people that look down on other supernaturals. They're encouraged to use their magic to bind subjects to study and analyze for their obsessions. Their very presence warps the world around them. Literally - their nimbus is pulling down parts of the Supernal and overwriting reality bit by bit, and you're slowly transforming people via Nimbus Tilt. Changelings, meanwhile, are defined by -fleeing- from the Gentry - magically privileged beings that shape the realm around them at whim. They're the ones that were the subjected to all the things that mages are inclined to do.<br /> <br /> In a very real way, the Awakened are like humanized versions of the Gentry. And changelings bear striking similarities to the entities that mages bind to their purpose. Now, at high Wisdom/Clarity, you can see the difference - both mages and changelings are still people, unlike the Gentry/bound spirits. However, the less Wise / perceptive lose sight of that, and the sympathy breaks down. Fate magic, by all rights, should be horrifying to changelings. The Lost rely on pledges being relatively consistant for mental stability. Mages can throw that out the window. Meanwhile, changelings are extremely slippery, avoiding magic and any attempts to hold them still for study.<br /> <br /> This all creates a far more complicated relationship than just meeting up and then possibly getting along after some misunderstandings at the nature of Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very extremely true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T17:25:52-08:00","id":1032398,"title":"","content":"Bit of thread necromancy but on the subject of the M!Arcadia versus C!Arcadia i've always interpreted the changeling arcadia as being a product of the lie, an imitiation born from the shadow of the lunargent tower. i've actually applied the same logic to the inferno, as well as the source of azoth, the shadow and the underworld. I Interpret the changeling's arcadia as a lower depth that feeds on Truth and thus devour dreams of the onieros. i've actually got an (as of yet unused) rule in my chronicle that summoning a supernal entity of fate or time causes changelings to gain clarity, another if they aid in the completion of a trial and ANOTHER if it is summoned in the hedge as the supernal truth exposes the illusion of arcadia and brings it's Lie into sharper definition. i've also determines that just being around supernal fey causes the (not so) True Fey to have a bit of an existential crisis, and makes them lash out at the entity. so if somehow a supernal verge was made in arcadia it would probably cause the Gentry to collectively shit themselves","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3729-darkfoxdev","name":"Darkfoxdev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T10:18:02-08:00","id":1032750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkfoxdev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032398#post1032398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of thread necromancy but on the subject of the M!Arcadia versus C!Arcadia i've always interpreted the changeling arcadia as being a product of the lie, an imitiation born from the shadow of the lunargent tower. i've actually applied the same logic to the inferno, as well as the source of azoth, the shadow and the underworld. I Interpret the changeling's arcadia as a lower depth that feeds on Truth and thus devour dreams of the onieros. i've actually got an (as of yet unused) rule in my chronicle that summoning a supernal entity of fate or time causes changelings to gain clarity, another if they aid in the completion of a trial and ANOTHER if it is summoned in the hedge as the supernal truth exposes the illusion of arcadia and brings it's Lie into sharper definition. i've also determines that just being around supernal fey causes the (not so) True Fey to have a bit of an existential crisis, and makes them lash out at the entity. so if somehow a supernal verge was made in arcadia it would probably cause the Gentry to collectively shit themselves</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling Arcadia definitely has the feel of a Lower Depth to me, taking into account how broad a catch-all that term can be. &quot;To the Fallen World as the Fallen World is to the Supernal&quot; seems like a decent description of the realms of the Gentry - petty worlds ruled by small gods and defined by supernatural lies that even the most ordinary human may recognize as such. The second edition Mage book even states that symbols from the Fallen World may take on great significance and power in the Lower Depths, which seems to be true of Changeling Arcadia. It's also a realm that can be distinguished from the mortal world latgely in terms of what it lacks - a realm without death, without growth, without any truths aside from those lies the Gentry decide to believe...<br /> <br /> This interpretation also has the advantage of making Changeling Arcadia a place mysterious and hostile to Mages, which they can only learn about second-hand. Most probably believe that, as with other Lower Depths, no one, Sleeper or Awakened, could possibly go there and return. And yet... Changelings do... and if a Mage were to discover that truth and accept that Changelings are more than just beings from the Lower Depths masquerading as something half-human, I'm sure that would become *very* curious very quickly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-16-2017, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:33:17-08:00","id":1032791,"title":"","content":"I'm very curious what critical component of existence you consider missing in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Nah, Arcadia is a parallel world to Ironside. Calling it a Lower Depth is like calling the Astral, the Shadow, or the Underworld a Lower Depth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:34:55-08:00","id":1032792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032791#post1032791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very curious what critical component of existence you consider missing in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Nah, Arcadia is a parallel world to Ironside. Calling it a Lower Depth is like calling the Astral, the Shadow, or the Underworld a Lower Depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>An argument could be made for a central lack of creativity, given that the Gentry can only steal and copy, bit it's a stretch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:45:13-08:00","id":1032800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032792#post1032792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An argument could be made for a central lack of creativity, given that the Gentry can only steal and copy, bit it's a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much a stretch, particularly given the summary Second Edition gave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T11:55:25-08:00","id":1032805,"title":"","content":"Humans produce glamour, which the Gentry cannot. Whatever that glamour is in truth, you can argue that the Gentry lack it,and thus are a &quot;lower depths.&quot; <br /> <br /> Of course, &quot;Lower Depths&quot; is nothing more than a mage-specific term that the Awakened use when trying to describe worlds and realms that they don't get. In the end, its nothing more than a convenient lable to toss on things they don't quite get, or match Supernal magic exactly. And, as a result, is ultimately meaningless beyond the idea fae don't fit into the Arcana nice and neatly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:14:44-08:00","id":1032817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032805#post1032805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans produce glamour, which the Gentry cannot. Whatever that glamour is in truth, you can argue that the Gentry lack it,and thus are a &quot;lower depths.&quot;<br /> <br /> Of course, &quot;Lower Depths&quot; is nothing more than a mage-specific term that the Awakened use when trying to describe worlds and realms that they don't get. In the end, its nothing more than a convenient lable to toss on things they don't quite get, or match Supernal magic exactly. And, as a result, is ultimately meaningless beyond the idea fae don't fit into the Arcana nice and neatly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, going off of how it's defined in Second Edition, that's not entirely true, and by that logic, the Shadow, Underworld, and Astral are Lower Depths, because these places are still Mysteries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:23:15-08:00","id":1032829,"title":"","content":"Even going by how its defined in 2e. Even with the whole &quot;because the region lacks even the energy to contain a unitary reality&quot; line. The closest thing to a definition we have is this:<br /> <br /> &quot;Each Lower Depth is unable to retain a critical constituent of existence; it\u2019s either absent, or has been distorted into something hostile to ordinary existence.&quot; <br /> <br /> Distorted from what, exactly? From some idealized form of existance that only exists in the human world? That's nothing more than human-centricism. Which admittedly is a huge theme of mage, but my point stands. Mages define what is or isn't a Lower Depth based on their notions of what should or should not exist. Its still an arbitrary line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-16-2017, 03:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:25:31-08:00","id":1032832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032829#post1032829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even going by how its defined in 2e. Even with the whole &quot;because the region lacks even the energy to contain a unitary reality&quot; line.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was more referring to the &quot;It lacks enough existing-existence that going there causes you to instantly die&quot; part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T12:40:29-08:00","id":1032846,"title":"","content":"From what I'm reading, that's not a given on all of them. And lets be fair - there was a realm described where Death didn't exist in it, so you won't instantly die there either. In fact, you can't die in that realm. Entering a realm without desire may very well eliminate one's desire to return home, and you'll eventually die as a result (likely starvation), but you won't spontaneously die as a result. *shrugs*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T14:47:39-08:00","id":1032927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032846#post1032846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I'm reading, that's not a given on all of them. And lets be fair - there was a realm described where Death didn't exist in it, so you won't instantly die there either. In fact, you can't die in that realm. Entering a realm without desire may very well eliminate one's desire to return home, and you'll eventually die as a result (likely starvation), but you won't spontaneously die as a result. *shrugs*</div> </div> </div> </div> You don't automatically die in the Inferno either, it's just nearly impossible to leave for none demons, someone has to open the door from the outside, but it's been stated to be a Lower Depth and the Strix Plane can also be visited by Vampric creatures like Ghouls and Kindred, without saying and if you move, fast enough you can even avoid dying, and its said to be a Lower Depth.<br /> <br /> I think that whole inhospitable to earthly life thing is a general rule, not a universal one.<br /> <br /> Hopefully Signs of Sorcery will clarity the Lower Depths and it's inhabitants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:07:42-08:00","id":1033011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032927#post1032927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hopefully Signs of Sorcery will clarity the Lower Depths and it's inhabitants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the book is dedicated to Mysteries that are Supernal? Doubt it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T17:42:09-08:00","id":1033043,"title":"","content":"Irregardless, I think that we do have enough examples where we -could- say that mages could consider Faerie to be part of the Lower Depths if the ST so desired. As I said, though, that's mostly a mage-specific term, and pretty much meaningless outside of an Awakening game. It has zero effect on changelings, or even anyone else, and only affects mages as trivia or potentially feeding into someone's Obsession.<br /> <br /> If it enables fun crossover plots (which it can) then it should all be for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-16-2017, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-16T18:58:09-08:00","id":1033089,"title":"","content":"I don't know much about Mage, but I like this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T00:53:16-08:00","id":1033212,"title":"","content":"Ironically, Lower Depths is mage term for 'Here will be Dragons' - places that do not work with Arcana the way Awakened are acustomed to. ( It's ironic as Dragons are universal Symbols of magic in Diamond Orders. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) On general note, Lower Depths also lacks some qualities realm need to 'feed' - in Changeling Arcadia they are probably emotions, that are changed by the realm in to Glamour that is sustaining it. In that way, True Fae <i>literally</i> need to cupture humans ( and change in to changelings by this ) to survive - or they need they stories told by mortals in material world. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T05:36:41-08:00","id":1033284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032805#post1032805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans produce glamour, which the Gentry cannot. Whatever that glamour is in truth, you can argue that the Gentry lack it,and thus are a &amp;quot;lower depths.&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> Of course, &amp;quot;Lower Depths&amp;quot; is nothing more than a mage-specific term that the Awakened use when trying to describe worlds and realms that they don't get. In the end, its nothing more than a convenient lable to toss on things they don't quite get, or match Supernal magic exactly. And, as a result, is ultimately meaningless beyond the idea fae don't fit into the Arcana nice and neatly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, it means something specific. Faerie is weird and hostile, but it doesn't <i>hunger</i> the way the Strix, Inferno, and Duat do. Faerie's most notable for being the source of things coming into the world, (and taking changelings to be in turn, but eh) not an endless black hole of taking. Mages don't call anything not the material, shadow, astral, or underworld a Depth.<br /> <br /> I dislike the whole &quot;shadow of Supernal Arcadia!&quot; Theory, too, as a) the Supernal Realms don't work like that and b) it's usually based on fanon fuelled by cosmological misunderstandings.<br /> <br /> Neat diagrams and easy &quot;off the map&quot; designations don't hold water in our complex modern CofD of jet-powered Deviants and time travel.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:29:30-08:00","id":1033345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033284#post1033284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah, it means something specific. Faerie is weird and hostile, but it doesn't <i>hunger</i> the way the Strix, Inferno, and Duat do. Faerie's most notable for being the source of things coming into the world, (and taking changelings to be in turn, but eh) not an endless black hole of taking. Mages don't call anything not the material, shadow, astral, or underworld a Depth.<br /> <br /> I dislike the whole &amp;quot;shadow of Supernal Arcadia!&amp;quot; Theory, too, as a) the Supernal Realms don't work like that and b) it's usually based on fanon fuelled by cosmological misunderstandings.<br /> <br /> Neat diagrams and easy &amp;quot;off the map&amp;quot; designations don't hold water in our complex modern CofD of jet-powered Deviants and time travel.</div> </div> </div> </div>God I want there to be a cosmology section in the Crossover Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T07:47:32-08:00","id":1033356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033284#post1033284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Faerie is weird and hostile, but it doesn't <i>hunger</i> the way the Strix, Inferno, and Duat do.</div> </div> </div> </div> Arguably. I personally think Faerie comes off as rather hungry. I think its coming off as hungrier than Duat, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-17-2017, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:26:20-08:00","id":1033439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033356#post1033356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Arguably. I personally think Faerie comes off as rather hungry. I think its coming off as hungrier than Duat, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Things so regularly come out of Faerie to the point that the borderland between it and Earth is the de facto otherworld of its parent game and the ability to open a gate to said borderland is a template feature of its associated magical being.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the three Lower Depths under discussion are consistently accessible only by:<br /> <br /> 1. Being in the company of one of the most potent members of a &quot;species&quot; that has to shed its potency if it would grow past the cap (and can voluntarily perform this shedding at any time).<br /> <br /> 2. Explicitly rare gateways that require rolls to exit or avoid entering, typically limited by the generation of truly prodigious amounts of atrocious resonance and/or leveraging the actions of mental/ephemeral parasites that are so unobtrusive they can masquerade as run-of-the-mill intrusive thoughts.<br /> <br /> 3. An afterlife that holds the waiting sacrifices to an oblivion-goddess which consumes the energies of relics borne by dreaming immortals who only wake for direct calls or an astrological convergence that happens less than once a millennium.<br /> <br /> A Lower Depth does not have <i>thoroughfares</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments"