03#post1033503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, can we say that Arcadia is as part of the Fallen World as the Shadow or the Underworld are? I mean, were it not for the fact that it's a 'line-exclusive' realm and that it's not a hungry lower realm lying further from the Fallen...<br /> <br /> Os is Arcadia in an entirely different 'cosmological league' and the actual &quot;fallen world realm&quot; is the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitively part of the Fallen World.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T14:20:12-08:00","id":1033637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yuukale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033503#post1033503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Os is Arcadia in an entirely different 'cosmological league' and the actual &quot;fallen world realm&quot; is the Hedge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that there potentially are realms other than the Supernal, Fallen and Lower Depths. For instance, the Principle (to the extent it exists) is it's own category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:29:02-08:00","id":1033832,"title":"","content":"I have to wonder why mages aren't more aware of/interested in Arcadia. Mages have been sticking their noses where they don't belong since at least the dawn of this iteration of human history, and yet it remains a huge blind spot for them. I mean, mages know that nobody who goes for a swim in the Ocean Orouboros ever comes back, presumably because more than a few mages over the centuries have *tried it*, and yet they still seem blissfully unaware of the Gentry and their realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 01-17-2017, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T19:44:30-08:00","id":1033836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033832#post1033832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder why mages aren't more aware of/interested in Arcadia.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's populated by a bunch of slave-taking gods and the land itself is actively hostile to the unaffiliated. That's usually reason enough to not dive into the depths of a magical realm without prep work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages have been sticking their noses where they don't belong since at least the dawn of this iteration of human history, and yet it remains a huge blind spot for them. </div> </div> </div>This is a bold assertion backed up by literally nothing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, mages know that nobody who goes for a swim in the Ocean Orouboros ever comes back, presumably because more than a few mages over the centuries have *tried it*, and yet they still seem blissfully unaware of the Gentry and their realms. </div> </div> </div>The Ocean Ouroboros is the farthest extreme of a realm that you reach through meditation and it's neighbors with the nearest Fallen equivalent of the <i>gods of the Arcana</i>. The fae are a comparatively niche interest that the larger body of Awakened society has nevertheless accumulated about as much lore on as anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T20:21:04-08:00","id":1033858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033832#post1033832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to wonder why mages aren't more aware of/interested in Arcadia. Mages have been sticking their noses where they don't belong since at least the dawn of this iteration of human history, and yet it remains a huge blind spot for them. I mean, mages know that nobody who goes for a swim in the Ocean Orouboros ever comes back, presumably because more than a few mages over the centuries have *tried it*, and yet they still seem blissfully unaware of the Gentry and their realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Odds are they have, but it is a pretty varied place. One mage can spend their entire life studying Arcadia only to find that they've only explored one realm. The Arcadia of Changeling is not a single unified area similar like the Hisil. It's more like the thousands of Places That Aren't in the Hisil.<br /> <br /> From there it would get harder to prove anything, as the Gentry vary from one to the next. Certainly the basics are known, it's not the Supernal Arcadia, it's a place of contracts and powerful alien beings, it has a warping affect on people, even mages, who stay there too long. Iron acts as a bane. That much could probably be taught by any mage who seems like they've been around and are well-studied. But even there, if you were a beginning mage who had no ties to Fate and didn't know or care about changelings and had never met one, is it something you would seek to learn about, compared to something more relevant?<br /> <br /> Then there's the geographical and chronological problem. Arcadia doesn't neatly overlap with the world the way the Shadow does. I think that may have been refined for the Hedge in second edition, with it reacting to pain or fear or something, but in first edition Arcadia didn't seem to correlate nicely with the real world. You could be taken by the Raptor in Chains in New York and find yourself a running hare next to what once was an Asian soldier stolen from the world four thousand years ago. The mages in Washington, at least those interested in the Shadow, likely know of the major spirit courts there, including the spirits of the city. But there's no 'Washington DC' Gentry that were limited to the city, though I guess there could be, and any other Gentry could pop up.<br /> <br /> Plus not as easy to really get to and explore.<br /> <br /> It's probably one of the more well known 'other planes' though. Less so than the Underworld and the Shadow but more than Duat.<br /> <br /> I'd expect we'll see some of the more well-spread beliefs about Arcadia when the Crossover book comes out. Until then, I believe the book Rites of Spring might details the general belief mages hold about Arcadia, or at least changelings. Maybe Equinox Road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-17-2017, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T20:36:22-08:00","id":1033866,"title":"","content":"The time-incongruities is still a thing.<br /> <br /> And who says that Mages don't poke around, or try at least? As parallel worlds go, it is harder to explore/devour the Mystery of, certainly, but mages do what mages do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 01-17-2017, 11:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T01:20:13-08:00","id":1033916,"title":"","content":"I assume that there are Changeling Experts in the Orders, probably Mastigos or Acanthus, who do explore the Hedge, deal with Freeholds, and patiently explain to apprentices that &quot;Arcadia&quot; is a Greek word misapplied to both Faerie and the Supernal Realm of Time.<br /> <br /> It's just that without a crossover section in a book, we haven't written about them. They've fallen into the comfortable Venn centre of &quot;the terminology is *just* this side of confusingly similar&quot;, &quot;the Hedge doesn't have the immediate use of the Underworld, Shadow, or Astral&quot; and &quot;Changeling 2e still isn't out so it's not worth writing about&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T04:48:52-08:00","id":1033958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033439#post1033439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lower Depth does not have <i>thoroughfares</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> Strix can make one to their realm for both strix to leave and at least vampires to freely enter. It seems to me that, for every rule that people come up with, there's exceptions to it. That makes this entire thing sound extremely arbitrary.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is a Lower Depth because we're not detailing it out for PCs to visit&quot; is the general vibe I'm getting. If someone wants to say that Faerie is a Lower Depths.... why say no? Why even bother forcing an answer that gets in the way of potential stories? In a game that's supposed to have an uncertain cosmology and full of mysteries, I really find such hard definitions that are being pushed to be... overly forced. To use another mage example, it feels like Left-Handed. Something is &quot;lower depths&quot; because some powers-that-be have decided to arbitrarily label it such, because it meets some semi-flexible criteria.<br /> <br /> Either way, I've made my point, and I'm out. Y'all do what's best for your individual stories, and game on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 01-18-2017, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T04:51:51-08:00","id":1033959,"title":"","content":"Honestly. I think any interactions between a changeling and a mage would be at least a little bit soiled by a guts deep all-consuming Envy, changelings lost the most important things in their life for their magic, and the mages just walk by, with great magical powers and not having to lose anything to gain them. They could be friends one time or two especially when they realize a mage will have to pay a very steep price sooner oor or later. but for most of the time? I think changelingss would want to kick mages ass just out of principle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4621,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","user":"Nicolas Milioni","date":". 01-18-2017, 07:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T08:03:12-08:00","id":1034017,"title":"","content":"Apparently some of them believe that mages are gifted by their powers by the True Fae, perhaps even being related to them. A fifth of them being sworn to Arcadia probably doesn't help dissuade that.<br /> <br /> For the general changeling, I'd expect mages would be seen with suspicion, dread and fear.<br /> <br /> After all, it's not like changelings all made a grasp for power that went badly, some of them seemed to have just gotten lucky enough to be kidnapped by a monster from an elder dimension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T09:05:52-08:00","id":1034047,"title":"","content":"A lot of it depends on how it goes down in the initial interactions. I don't think a lot of mages go around parading &quot;I'm an Arcadian Mage&quot;, and the most obvious place where the &quot;seeing fairies&quot; thing is going to happen is when they use Mage Sight, and so it comes down to just how they talk about it.<br /> <br /> There's enough evidence for both sides to realize that the other is not talking about the same Arcadia, and it by and large is dependent on how such evidence manifests and how the other side takes it.<br /> <br /> But changelings aren't stupid, and are probably less prone to the &quot;FREAK OUT, ACANTHUS!&quot; response than expected, because there is enough evidence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:15:14-08:00","id":1034126,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I'm sure at least a few Changelings *are* stupid, and a lot more are paranoid. Plus, considering the potentially deadly significance of exact wording in Fey magic, im guessing very few Changelings are going to just shrug it off when Acanthus mages talk about their powers being linked to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> That said, mages and Changelings are both very diverse groups, and I'd be hesitant to make any broad statements at all about their interactions, save that, as with all things supernatural, there will always be mages who want to poke and prod and try to figure out how Changelings work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T11:31:14-08:00","id":1034133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033958#post1033958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Strix can make one to their realm for both strix to leave and at least vampires to freely enter.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Strix can make <i>a portal</i>. Faerie has <i>literal stable roads running between it and Earth</i>. These things are not interchangeable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In a game that's supposed to have an uncertain cosmology and full of mysteries, I really find such hard definitions that are being pushed to be... overly forced. </div> </div> </div>The way entrances to Lower Depths operate is described in Mage's section on Irises. It's not even remotely descriptively comparable to how a Hedge gate works.<br /> <br /> The fact that many Lower Depths are defined by outright missing the qualities that allow certain Arcana to function does little to quell the sense that some people are pushing &quot;Faerie is a Lower Depth&quot; as part of the Changeling fandom's ongoing baggage with Mage, particularly since &quot;Awakened magic doesn't work at all in the Hedge&quot; is a misreading I have seen multiple times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To use another mage example, it feels like Left-Handed. Something is &quot;lower depths&quot; because some powers-that-be have decided to arbitrarily label it such, because it meets some semi-flexible criteria. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Left-Handed&quot; is a partially politicized term for a general umbrella of harmful practices relating to the use of Awakened magic. A Lower Depth is a place that is so far removed from Phenomenal reality that parts of the latter start to fail around gates to the former and these failures are lesser symptoms of the place's inhospitability to conventional existence.<br /> <br /> The Fae literally <i>cannot make</i> worlds that are uniformly inhospitable to visitors, and the Fae <i>are</i> Faerie. Their need to enforce narrative upon themselves and their surroundings is not interchangeable with the consumptive hunger common to the Depths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T14:27:07-08:00","id":1034245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1010017#post1010017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I'm having a headache about an Arcadian Verge in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> You people are not good people.</div> </div> </div> </div> It gets worse: Verges often have Irises connecting them to Emanation Realms. What kind of Emanation would you find through an Arcadian Verge in Faerie?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-18T16:08:42-08:00","id":1034308,"title":"","content":"I can see some combinations of Courts and Orders going well, like Winter + Guardians Of The Veil, Summer + Adamatine Arrow and Autumn + Mysterium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T01:31:37-08:00","id":1034485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1034308#post1034308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see some combinations of Courts and Orders going well, like Winter + Guardians Of The Veil, Summer + Adamatine Arrow and Autumn + Mysterium.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's basiclly how I run it from 1E - IF local Orders and Seasonal Courts have diplomatic relations, they quickly find out they work with many the same Modus Operandi and can learn a large chunks from one another. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T06:07:23-08:00","id":1034545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1032792#post1032792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An argument could be made for a central lack of creativity, given that the Gentry can only steal and copy, bit it's a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Stability? Going back to what MCN said about changelings needing their pledges and contracts to stay consistent for the sake of their own stability. Maybe the realm and its natives themselves need that, and that's why they have to take people - they need outside parties to sign into their deals for their deals to make an even vaguely coherent existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033284#post1033284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dislike the whole &quot;shadow of Supernal Arcadia!&quot; Theory, too, as a) the Supernal Realms don't work like that and b) it's usually based on fanon fuelled by cosmological misunderstandings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disliked it because it made Mage's Fae truer than Changeling's True Fae (and was thus way more Mage-supremacist than One-Arcadia ever was, given that One-Arcadia by definition questioned mages' interpretation of the Supernal World itself).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033491#post1033491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that's there is a photo of all the writers pointing and laughing at the reader.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. A Cossover Chronicle that doesn't address making crossover cosmologies is failing in its purpose (well one of it's purposes). The only thing that needs pointing and laughing at is the idea that connections between game-lines' cosmologies means that one of them wins in some way.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:16:32-08:00","id":1034816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1033916#post1033916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume that there are Changeling Experts in the Orders, probably Mastigos or Acanthus, who do explore the Hedge, deal with Freeholds, and patiently explain to apprentices that &amp;quot;Arcadia&amp;quot; is a Greek word misapplied to both Faerie and the Supernal Realm of Time.<br /> <br /> It's just that without a crossover section in a book, we haven't written about them. They've fallen into the comfortable Venn centre of &amp;quot;the terminology is *just* this side of confusingly similar&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;the Hedge doesn't have the immediate use of the Underworld, Shadow, or Astral&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;Changeling 2e still isn't out so it's not worth writing about&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div> I find it curious that you say that the Hedge doesn't have the immediate use of the Underworld, Astral, or, Shadow. <br /> <br /> I curious as to what impedes Mages from using the Hedge the way they do The Shadow, The Underworld, and the Astral? <br /> <br /> Perhaps that inhabitants of the Hedge don't use essence? Or it's harder to exit the Hedge for Mages? Or is the Hedge simple more dangerous to Mages then the others? Or a mix of all three reasons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:18:25-08:00","id":1034818,"title":"","content":"Maybe Arcadia and the Hedge is the Upper Depths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:31:25-08:00","id":1034831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1034816#post1034816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it curious that you say that the Hedge doesn't have the immediate use of the Underworld, Astral, or, Shadow.<br /> <br /> I curious as to what impedes Mages from using the Hedge the way they do The Shadow, The Underworld, and the Astral?</div> </div> </div> </div>No spell that opens to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps that inhabitants of the Hedge don't use essence? Or it's harder to exit the Hedge for Mages? Or is the Hedge simple more dangerous to Mages then the others? Or a mix of all three reasons? </div> </div> </div>They tend to use Glamour, they're not ephemera. And, at least in first edition, you couldn't use magic to escape the Hedge. It was as dangerous in the Hedge as it was to everyone, as everyone could find themselves overwhelmed and absorbed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T13:37:12-08:00","id":1034834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1034831#post1034831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No spell that opens to Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> They tend to use Glamour, they're not ephemera. And, at least in first edition, you couldn't use magic to escape the Hedge. It was as dangerous in the Hedge as it was to everyone, as everyone could find themselves overwhelmed and absorbed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn I never thought of the fact say the Fate Arcana can't simple open a portal or teleport a Mage to Arcadia, and even the Hedge can just be access with a spell, although not as hostile to Mages or hard to access as Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T14:41:06-08:00","id":1034870,"title":"","content":"Fate could probably be used to open an <i>existing </i>door to the Hedge, since those can be opened by the right circumstances to begin with.<br /> <br /> I'm unsure about teleportation, I don't know the rules about it at all but maybe if you had a previous connection to someplace in the Hedge and it still existed you could teleport to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T18:01:47-08:00","id":1034972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1034870#post1034870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate could probably be used to open an <i>existing </i>door to the Hedge, since those can be opened by the right circumstances to begin with.<br /> <br /> I'm unsure about teleportation, I don't know the rules about it at all but maybe if you had a previous connection to someplace in the Hedge and it still existed you could teleport to it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Maybe, but you still can't do that with Arcadia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:11:29-08:00","id":1035532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1009776-how-do-changelings-and-mages-feel-about-each-other?p=1034816#post1034816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it curious that you say that the Hedge doesn't have the immediate use of the Underworld, Astral, or, Shadow.<br /> <br /> I curious as to what impedes Mages from using the Hedge the way they do The Shadow, The Underworld, and the Astral?<br /> <br /> Perhaps that inhabitants of the Hedge don't use essence? Or it's harder to exit the Hedge for Mages? Or is the Hedge simple more dangerous to Mages then the others? Or a mix of all three reasons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Mage magic explicitly comes from the soul, and the Brambles tear up the soul pretty bad. On top of that, unless I'm mistaken, the Hedge can't be left without a proper exit (in essence, by entering the Hedge, you made an agreement with it to leave properly), so magic can't get you out like it might from other realms. On top of that, things like space, time, and matter get really wonky there, so that's three very useful Arcana borked to high heaven. Then, you're in the fringes of home turf for what's functionally gods of Fate, so playing with Fate magic is pretty dangerous, too. Spirit is of extremely limited use, there, since there's no Twilight and spirits that get stuck there often end up becoming Hobgoblins instead. That's about half the Arcana made weaker, more difficult or more dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T17:22:52-08:00","id":1035541,"title":"","content":"Now I kinda want to write a Mind/Fate legacy called the Hedgewalkers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}